Mars Has a Clingy Moon (sequel to The Moon Is Slowly Breaking Up With Us) — flat-vector explainer (1080×1920, 24 fps)
Everything on screen is drawn in code (main.js, canvas 2D): Mars, Phobos, Deimos, Earth and the Moon as characters, the rover, the eclipse, the type.
No images, no stock footage, no generated media. Our own character designs; style grammar inspired by flat-vector science
channels, nothing copied. Facts: the fact table in SCRIPT.md (NASA, NASA Goddard, JPL, Black & Mittal 2015).

Type
  Nunito — Vernon Adams, Jacques Le Bailly and the Nunito Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-Nunito.txt),
  from github.com/google/fonts.
Voice
  Kokoro-82M (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george, lang en-gb. Word timings from faster-whisper small.en (MIT). Run by voice_kokoro.py.
Score and sound effects
  Original, synthesized in music.py and mix.py (numpy/scipy). No samples.
